PostgreSQL setup for ProxyFlow (Linux / Bash)
=============================================

The repository's docker-compose.yml defines a PostgreSQL 15 container named
gateway-postgres. Its database is proxyflow, the application role is dbo, the
container port is 5432, and the host port is 5433. Its data is persisted in the
postgres_data Docker volume.

Recommended: run only the database container
--------------------------------------------
From the repository root:

    docker compose up -d postgres
    docker compose ps
    docker compose exec -T postgres pg_isready -U dbo -d proxyflow

Initialize or update the log schema using the idempotent SQL scripts:

    docker compose exec -T postgres psql -U dbo -d proxyflow -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 < Gateway.Api/Database/Models/Scripts/Script1.sql
    docker compose exec -T postgres psql -U dbo -d proxyflow -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 < Gateway.Api/Database/Models/Scripts/Script2.sql

Connect from this host with psql:

    psql -h localhost -p 5433 -U dbo -d proxyflow

The password is configured by POSTGRES_PASSWORD in docker-compose.yml. Do not
use the sample development credentials in production.

Run the API as a container for local development
------------------------------------------------
The container reaches PostgreSQL by the Compose service name postgres on port
5432. The frontend on this host expects the API at localhost:5025:

    ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development API_HOST_PORT=5025 docker compose up -d --build

This starts both the database and API containers. Swagger is available at
http://localhost:5025/swagger/index.html. To start only the API after starting
the database, run:

    ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development API_HOST_PORT=5025 docker compose up -d --build gateway-api

Run the API directly on the host instead
----------------------------------------
When the API runs on the host, connect it to the database's published host port
(5433), not the container-only port (5432). Supply a valid connection string
through the ASP.NET Core configuration environment variable:

    ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection='Host=localhost;Port=5433;Database=proxyflow;Username=dbo;Password=YOUR_DB_PASSWORD' ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development dotnet run --project Gateway.Api/Gateway.Api.csproj --urls http://localhost:5025

In another terminal, run the React development server:

    cd gateway-ui
    npm install
    npm run dev

Browser URLs:
    Frontend: http://localhost:5173/
    Backend Swagger: http://localhost:5025/swagger/index.html

Useful database/container commands
----------------------------------

    docker compose logs -f postgres
    docker compose exec postgres psql -U dbo -d proxyflow
    docker compose stop postgres
    docker compose start postgres

Stopping containers does not delete the postgres_data volume. Do not run
"docker compose down -v" unless you explicitly intend to permanently delete
the database volume and its data.
